<section class="panel">
	<div class="wrap">
		<div class="eyebrow">Route 2 &middot; keeps your data</div>
		<h1>On a phone already running postmarketOS</h1>
		<p class="lede">Three commands on the phone. Works on a stock
		<code>qcom-sm7150</code> install with Plasma Mobile and systemd.</p>
	</div>
</section>

<section>
	<div class="wrap">
		<div class="h"><span>01</span><h2>Add it</h2></div>
		<div class="sh">
			<div class="bar"><i></i><span>ON THE PHONE</span></div>
			<pre>sudo wget -qO /etc/apk/keys/@KEY@ @URL@/keys/@KEY@
echo @URL@/main | sudo tee -a /etc/apk/repositories
sudo apk update
sudo apk add utsugi-surya-base</pre>
		</div>
		<p>Untagged, on purpose. A tagged line makes apk prefer upstream for every
		dependency and the patched packages silently lose.</p>
		<div class="scroll">
		<table>
			<tr><th class="mono">utsugi-surya-base</th><td>The phone: kernel, hardware,
			Plasma fixes, six apps.</td></tr>
			<tr><th class="mono">utsugi-surya-extras</th><td>Optional: browser, mail,
			two-factor, social, photos. <a href="packages.html">Listed here</a>.</td></tr>
		</table>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="panel">
	<div class="wrap">
		<div class="h"><span>02</span><h2>Then reboot &mdash; deliberately</h2></div>
		<div class="note"><i></i><div>
			<b>The kernel comes with it, and a kernel that does not boot is a reboot
			loop.</b> The watchdog fires 20&nbsp;s after PID&nbsp;1 and there is no
			screen left to fix it from. Have a way back in before you reboot:
			<a href="https://github.com/utsugi-pmos/utsugi-pmaports/blob/main/flash/surya.md">flash/surya.md</a>.
		</div></div>
		<p>From then on <code>sudo apk upgrade</code> keeps everything current,
		kernel included.</p>
		<div class="next">
			<a href="devices.html"><b>Read</b><span>What does not work</span></a>
			<a href="install-image.html"><b>Or</b><span>Just flash the image</span></a>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
